{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Go, eat.</b> This is speech of the heart of the children of man, and it is folly. The matter is: after the dead have no portion in the world, while you are alive — go, eat your bread in joy, and drink your wine with a good heart, for these deeds Elohim desires that you do."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:37.994186695Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}